# Mutation plan for the channel and team membership plugin hook sites —
# `crates/mm-app/src/plugin_hooks.rs`, `crates/mm-app/src/channel_member.rs` and
# `crates/mm-app/src/team_member.rs` (docs/PLUGIN_PLAN.md, Phase 5).
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/plugin-hooks-membership.plan
#
# The oracle is `parity::plugin_hooks::the_membership_hooks_fire_as_go_fires_them`: one plugin
# binary under a real Go host and under the Rust host, the same client action against each, and
# the two transcripts diffed field for field. So a line here either changes what the plugin was
# handed, or changes what the client got back when the plugin refused.
#
# Not mutated: the caller names (`Where` is `json:"-"`), the `Reason` parameter name (Go's
# translation is the only thing that reads it and [D-092] means our `message` is the id anyway),
# and the space-channel guard on `ChannelMemberWillBeAdded` (no route on this deployment creates
# one). The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.

